{"embedding_dim": 1024, "data": [{"__id__": "doc-f2259393bbdc5e950df79a0ed459d818-chunk-000", "__created_at__": 1784284306, "content": "PT  Rafita  Product  Launch  and  Bundling  Strategy  -  Q3  2026  \nThis  document  outlines  the  strategic  bundling  and  promotional  plans  for  Q3  2026.  The  \nstrategies\n \nbelow\n \nare\n \ndesigned\n \nto\n \noptimize\n \nour\n \ncurrent\n \ninventory\n \nlisted\n \nin\n \nthe\n \nPT\n \nRafita\n \nProduct\n \nand\n \nPrice\n \nCatalog.\n  \n1.  Strategic  Product  Bundles  \nTo  increase  the  average  order  value  and  move  lower-stock  items  alongside  high-stock  items,  we  \nare\n \nintroducing\n \nthe\n \nfollowing\n \npackages:\n ●  The  WFH  Pro  Kit:  Designed  for  remote  workers.  This  bundle  includes  the  Rafita  \nMechanical\n \nKeyboard\n \n(RAF-KBD-MECH)\n,\n \nRafita\n \nOffice\n \nDesk\n \nMat\n \n(RAF-MAT-01)\n,\n \nand\n \nRafita\n \nFast\n \nCharger\n \n65W\n \n(RAF-CHG-65)\n.\n \nNote:\n \nDue\n \nto\n \nthe\n \nmechanical\n \nkeyboard's\n \nlimited\n \nstock\n \n(85\n \nunits),\n \nthis\n \nbundle\n \nwill\n \nbe\n \ncapped\n \nat\n \n50\n \npackages.\n ●  The  Urban  Commuter:  Targeted  at  students  and  daily  commuters.  This  package  \ncombines\n \nthe\n \nRafita\n \nBackpack\n \nNeo\n \n(RAF-BPK-NEO)\n \nand\n \nthe\n \nRafita\n \nTumbler\n \nSwiss\n \nEdition\n \n(RAF-TMB-SW)\n.\n \nWe\n \nhave\n \nample\n \nstock\n \n(over\n \n200\n \nunits\n \neach),\n \nso\n \nthis\n \nwill\n \nbe\n \nour\n \nmain\n \nvolume\n \ndriver.\n ●  The  Audio-Active  Set:  A  pairing  of  the  Rafita  Smartwatch  V1  (RAF-SMW-01)  and  Rafita  \nWireless\n \nEarbuds\n \n(RAF-TWS-01)\n \nfor\n \nfitness\n \nenthusiasts.\n  \n2.  Exclusive  VIP  Campaign  \nWe  currently  hold  exactly  60  units  of  the  Rafita  Smart  Home  Hub  (RAF-HUB-01) .  Instead  of  a  \ngeneral\n \nrelease,\n \nwe\n \nwill\n \nposition\n \nthis\n \nas\n \nan\n \nultra-premium\n \nitem.\n ●  Channel:  Email  Marketing.  ●  Target:  Top  100  members  of  the  \"Rafita  Closer\"  loyalty  program.  ●  Offer:  Early  access  to  the  Smart  Home  Hub  before  public  release.   \n3.  Channel  Allocation  &  Budget  Focus  \nBased  on  our  past  performance,  we  will  allocate  our  marketing  budget  for  these  bundles  as  \nfollows:\n \nBundle  Name  Primary  Marketing  Channel  Target  Demographic  \n  \nThe  WFH  Pro  Kit  Google  Ads  (Search)  Professionals,  Tech  Enthusiasts  \nThe  Urban  Commuter  TikTok  &  Instagram  Ads  Students,  Millennials  \n \n4.  Logistics  &  Supply  Chain  Integration  \nOrder  fulfillment  for  Eastern  Indonesia  will  be  prioritized  through  the  new  Makassar  logistics  \nhub.\n \nThe\n \nUrban\n \nCommuter\n \nbundle\n \nwill\n \nhave\n \n30%\n \nof\n \nits\n \ndedicated\n \nstock\n \npre-positioned\n \nat\n \nthe\n \nMakassar\n \nhub\n \nby\n \nAugust\n \n2026\n \nto\n \nensure\n \nfast\n \ndelivery.", "full_doc_id": "doc-f2259393bbdc5e950df79a0ed459d818", "file_path": "PT Rafita Product Launch and Bundling Strategy - Q3 2026.pdf", "vector": ""}, {"__id__": "doc-204c4010c5e21e4bedd9611af5fc5e77-chunk-000", "__created_at__": 1784284388, "content": "PT  Rafita  Marketing  Team  Performance  \nReport\n \nPeriod:  Quarter  1  (Q1)  2026  Prepared  By:  PT  Rafita  Internal  Marketing  Team   \n1.  Executive  Summary  \nThis  report  summarizes  the  performance  of  the  PT  Rafita  marketing  team  during  Quarter  1  of  \n2026.\n \nThe\n \nmain\n \nfocus\n \nduring\n \nthis\n \nperiod\n \nwas\n \nincreasing\n \nbrand\n \nawareness\n \nthrough\n \ndigital\n \ncampaigns\n \nand\n \nthe\n \nlaunch\n \nof\n \na\n \ncustomer\n \nloyalty\n \nprogram.\n \nOverall,\n \nkey\n \ntargets\n \nwere\n \nachieved\n \nwith\n \nseveral\n \nmetrics\n \nexceeding\n \ninitial\n \nexpectations\n \ndue\n \nto\n \noptimization\n \nacross\n \nseveral\n \ndigital\n \nchannels.\n  \n2.  Key  Achievements  \n●  35%  increase  in  organic  website  traffic  compared  to  the  previous  quarter.  ●  Social  media  follower  growth  (Instagram  and  TikTok)  of  15,000  new  followers  through  \norganic\n \nand\n \npaid\n \nefforts.\n ●  Cost  Per  Acquisition  (CPA)  decreased  by  12%  through  ad  targeting  strategy  optimization.  ●  Successful  launch  of  the  \"Rafita  Closer\"  campaign  which  generated  5,000  new  potential  \nleads.\n  \n3.  Campaign  Performance  Metrics  \nBelow  is  the  performance  breakdown  of  the  various  main  marketing  channels  run  during  Q1  \n2026:\n  Marketing  Channel   \nAllocated  Budget  (IDR)   \nLeads  Generated   \nConversion  Rate  (%)   \nROI  (%)    \nSocial  Media  Ads  (Meta  &  TikTok)   \n50.000.000  2.500  4.5%  120%  \nSearch  Engine  Marketing  (Google  Ads)  \n30.000.000  1.800  6.2%  145%  \nMarketing  Channel   \nAllocated  Budget  (IDR)   \nLeads  Generated   \nConversion  Rate  (%)   \nROI  (%)    \n \nEmail  Marketing   \n10.000.000  700  3.1%  80%  \n \n4.  Obstacle  Analysis  \n●  The  bounce  rate  on  the  \"Rafita  Closer\"  promotion  landing  page  was  still  quite  high  in  the  \nfirst\n \nweek\n \nof\n \nlaunch\n \n(reaching\n \n65%)\n \nbefore\n \nits\n \nspeed\n \nwas\n \noptimized.\n ●  Limited  visual  design  assets  caused  delays  in  the  A/B  testing  process  for  social  media  \nads.\n  \n5.  Follow-up  Plan  (Q2  2026)  \nBased  on  Q1  performance  analysis  results,  here  are  the  strategic  focuses  for  the  next  quarter:  1.  Increase  budget  allocation  for  Search  Engine  Marketing  by  20%  to  maximize  high  ROI  \nmomentum.\n 2.  Restructure  the  creative  asset  creation  workflow  so  that  the  A/B  testing  process  can  run  \nfaster.\n 3.  Optimize  email  marketing  segmentation  based  on  customer  behavior  to  increase  open  \nrates.\n 4.  Establish  strategic  partnerships  with  3-5  local  micro-influencers  to  expand  specific  market  \nreach.", "full_doc_id": "doc-204c4010c5e21e4bedd9611af5fc5e77", "file_path": "Laporan Kinerja Tim Marketing PT Rafita - Q1 2026.pdf", "vector": ""}], "matrix": ""}